{"id":"amram","name":"Amram","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:amram"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Amram","text":"Kindred of the High; i.e., “friend of Jehovah.” (1.) The son of Kohath, the son of Levi. He married Jochebed, “his father’s sister,” and was the father of Aaron, Miriam, and Moses (Ex. 6:18, 20; Num. 3:19). He died in Egypt at the age of 137 years (Ex. 6:20). His descendants were called Amramites (Num. 3:27; 1 Chr. 26:23). (2.) Ezra 10:34."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H6019","lemma":"עַמְרָם","xlit":"ʻAmrâm","gloss":"Amram, the name of two Israelites","kjv":"Amram","count":10,"share":0.71},{"strong":"H6955","lemma":"קְהָת","xlit":"Qᵉhâth","gloss":"Kehath, an Israelite","kjv":"Kohath","count":6,"share":0.43},{"strong":"H3324","lemma":"יִצְהָר","xlit":"Yitshâr","gloss":"Jitshar, an Israelite","kjv":"Izhar","count":4,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H5816","lemma":"עֻזִּיאֵל","xlit":"ʻUzzîyʼêl","gloss":"Uzziel, the name of six Israelites","kjv":"Uzziel","count":4,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H2276","lemma":"חֶבְרוֹנִי","xlit":"Chebrôwnîy","gloss":"Chebronite , an inhabitant of Chebron","kjv":"Hebronites","count":3,"share":0.21},{"strong":"H2275","lemma":"חֶבְרוֹן","xlit":"Chebrôwn","gloss":"Chebron, a place in Palestine, also the name of two Isra","kjv":"Hebron","count":4,"share":0.29}],"verses":["Exod.6.18","Exod.6.20","Num.3.19","Num.26.58","Num.26.59","1Chr.6.3","1Chr.6.18","1Chr.23.12","1Chr.23.13","Ezra.10.34","Exod.20.0","Num.3.27","1Chr.1.41","1Chr.26.23"],"related":[{"id":"kohath","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.313,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"izhar","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.167,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"hebron","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.041,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"aaron","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.027,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"kohath","type":"lexical","strong":"H6019","why":"both lead